/P 288 0 R
/E (I actually enjoyed Waterfall model more as a team because we don't go back and change ideas, style guides or anything in general. Compared to Agile, this is a lot easier to work with as we set the ideas and designs in the beginning and have to stick to it throughout the whole project. Even though there is less flexibility, as someone who hates going back and forth on concepts I definitely prefer the Waterfall model over Agile.)
/Pg 46 0 R
/K [4]
>>
